#: templates/report.html.j2:155
msgid "What CR_eff means — and what it does not"
msgstr "What CR_eff means — and what it does not"

#: templates/report.html.j2:157
msgid ""
"<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal the loop pushed in\n"
"    into an \"effectively used\" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal)</code>."
msgstr ""
"<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal the loop pushed in\n"
"    into an \"effectively used\" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal)</code>."

#: templates/report.html.j2:159
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Example %(label)s: %(cho)s g on\n"
"    (%(bol)s U bolus + %(loop)s U loop) ≈ <b>%(cre)s</b>\n"
"    instead of the configured ratio."
msgstr ""
"Example %(label)s: %(cho)s g on\n"
"    (%(bol)s U bolus + %(loop)s U loop) ≈ <b>%(cre)s</b>\n"
"    instead of the configured ratio."

#: templates/report.html.j2:161
#, python-format
msgid ""
"And even then the BG at\n"
"    %(w)s is still <b>%(d4)s %(unit)s</b> above baseline — the loop-boosted amount\n"
"    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound here</b>: the actually needed CR\n"
"    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units)."
msgstr ""
"And even then the BG at\n"
"    %(w)s is still <b>%(d4)s %(unit)s</b> above baseline — the loop-boosted amount\n"
"    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound here</b>: the actually needed CR\n"
"    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units)."

#: templates/report.html.j2:165
msgid ""
"<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude (\"rather tighter, roughly this much\") —\n"
"    <b>not</b> \"set the CR exactly to this value\". <b>Why only an approximation:</b> it assumes the\n"
"    loop extra belongs entirely to the meal (ignores correction of pre-existing highs, exercise,\n"
"    adaptation); the derived CR may contain blended-in corrections; single-window view.\n"
"    Therefore: read off direction + rough magnitude, decide the step small and iteratively with the team\n"
"    and re-measure every ~1–2 weeks."
msgstr ""
"<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude (\"rather tighter, roughly this much\") —\n"
"    <b>not</b> \"set the CR exactly to this value\". <b>Why only an approximation:</b> it assumes the\n"
"    loop extra belongs entirely to the meal (ignores correction of pre-existing highs, exercise,\n"
"    adaptation); the derived CR may contain blended-in corrections; single-window view.\n"
"    Therefore: read off direction + rough magnitude, decide the step small and iteratively with the team\n"
"    and re-measure every ~1–2 weeks."

